    "# Repaint an avatar texture from a reference picture\n**VTube Pro workflow, 16 GB graphics card** (Z-Image-Turbo + FLUX.2 klein 4B). Pack 2026.10.01.\n\nYour model's texture sheet repainted in the colours and materials of a character picture. Every seam stays where it is.\n\n## How to use it\n1. Load your texture sheet (the PNG from your model) in \"Your texture\".\n2. Load a picture of the character in \"Your reference\".\n3. Change the words if you like, then press Run.\n4. Find the result in ComfyUI's **output/VTubePro** folder (or right-click the picture > Save Image).\n\nThe **green boxes** are the ones to change.\n\n**You get:** A PNG the same size as your texture. Save it as a new file; keep the original.\n\n**In VTube Pro:** Open your model in Blender (or the costume editor), swap the texture for the new PNG and check it from every side. For whole-model paint by camera views, VTube Pro's own painter (Create tab, \"Paint with AI\") does more.\n\n**Settings:** 4 steps (distilled), CFG 1.\n\n## Models (all allow commercial use)\n- [flux-2-klein-4b.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein) (7.8 GB) in `models/diffusion_models`: Apache-2.0 (the 4B only; FLUX.2 klein 9B is non-commercial)\n- [qwen_3_4b.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo) (8.0 GB) in `models/text_encoders`: Apache-2.0\n- [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein) (0.3 GB) in `models/vae`: Apache-2.0\n\nMissing a model? ComfyUI offers to download it when you open this workflow. Or ask your AI: \n*\"Set up the VTube Pro avatar texture repaint workflow in ComfyUI\"*: the VTube Pro Helper downloads every file from its official page, checks it, and adds this workflow, after you say yes.\n\n## Tips\n- Faces stay hand-drawn: repaint clothes and hair, then fix the face by hand.\n- If a seam moved, lower \"denoise\" (small) or say \"keep every line\" (medium, large).\n- Run it when you are not live.\n- Make pictures when you are not live: picture AI slows face tracking."
   ],
